<BaseLayout title="Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement" current="/implementation-enablement/" description="Richard Allen's transferable experience in software migrations, onboarding, training, release validation, system transitions, documentation, and enablement.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Implementation, Onboarding & Enablement</div><h1>Help people adopt change with less friction.</h1><p class="lede">My experience is strongest where implementation connects customers, support teams, documentation, training, software validation, systems changes, and day-to-day adoption.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container grid two">
  <article class="card"><h3>HawkSoft online migration</h3><p>Project-managed/coordinated customer database moves between local networks and HawkSoft Online and helped move hundreds of users from a prior online service to a substantially improved one, supporting customers through the technical, workflow, and training transition.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>HawkSoft accounting-software redesign</h3><p>Led staff readiness for a major accounting-software change: communicated expectations six months in advance, arranged biweekly developer/staff education during the final two months, provided extra support and access to developers/management at go-live, and continued training for months afterward.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Kotter software build validation</h3><p>For new Bridge by Kotter builds, performed a systematic run-through of the software to confirm new functionality worked as intended and existing functionality had not been broken by the change. After releases, wrote procedure documentation and created several instructional YouTube videos showing customers how to use Bridge.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Shady Grove systems modernization</h3><p>Helped replace an older DOS-based X-ray film tracking system with a new system, contributing to an approximately 30% efficiency improvement. Also helped create the processes and procedures used to digitize thousands of X-ray films.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Willamette Broadband billing transition</h3><p>Was key in transitioning the company to a new billing system while handling customer service, billing, scheduling, troubleshooting, complaints, and customer training.</p></article>
  <article class="card"><h3>Training & enablement</h3><p>Trained customers and staff on software workflows, troubleshooting, features, product changes, and best practices; created or contributed to training documentation, presentations, webinars, onboarding materials, SOPs, staff communications, and customer-facing instructional content.</p></article>
</div></section>
<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><p class="small"><strong>Scope note:</strong> This page describes transferable implementation, onboarding, enablement, and software-release validation experience. It does not claim product-roadmap ownership, formal requirements ownership, or a dedicated Implementation Manager title.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
